# Berserk's "only before the combat damage step" is the turn's first combat phase's (CR 506.8d). Combat Celebrant's exertion adds
# a combat phase; Berserk is cast in the first combat's declare attackers step, then Merciful Mandate, paid in part with Llanowar
# Elves, ends that combat before its damage step, skipping its end of combat step (CR 724.2d-e). The Mandate untapped the Elves,
# so a second Berserk could be paid for, but the first combat is over all the same, so in the added combat's beginning of
# combat step it is refused.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Combat Celebrant
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Llanowar Elves
Berserk
Berserk
Merciful Mandate
Plains x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Combat Celebrant.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Combat Celebrant)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Berserk.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Combat Celebrant)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Merciful Mandate.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
! Bot1.Hand.Berserk.Cast
[Expect]
Step = BeginCombat
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Hand = Berserk
